rities of  varying types to be harassed by overly  obsessed fans of their work bates  portrays that mentality with ample gusto  balancing both manic cheerfulness and  bloodthirsty rage it was no surprise  when at the subsequent 63rd academy  awards bates took home an oscar for  actress in a leading role  stephen king definitely has a knack for  creating memorable female antagonists  and rose the hat is no exception dr  sleep the sequel to the shining picks up  30 years after danny torrance  experienced the horrors of the overlook  hotel as dany copes with both his  sobriety and his shining ability a new  threat looms it's revealed that people  with the shining have become victims to  a vampiric cult known as the true knot  the cult led by rose the hat maintains  immortality by consuming the essence of  shining users the film centers on dany's  fight to protect a young girl named abra  and her gift from rose despite being the  leader of a vicious group of vampiric  monsters rose is not a one-note villain  she legitimately cares for her clan and  is heartbroken when one of their  immortalities finally expires however  the film never lets you forget just how  cruel and sadistic rose actually is at  her core the most horrific example being  a scene when rose and true not kill a  young boy for his essence she explains  that the essence grows stale as people  age which is why her clan targets  children rebecca ferguson received much  praise for her portrayal of rose the hat  injecting the role with equal parts  malice and charisma  behind every psychotic serial killing  doll there is an equally psychotic  serial killing woman in the case of  charles lee ray also known as chucky  that would be tiffany valentine who was  first introduced and bride of chucky  retroactively created as chucky's  equally bloodthirsty girlfriend tiffany  succeeds at resurrecting him after his  gruesome demise in child's play 3. what  begins as a joyous if not bloody reunion  quickly goes south as chucky reveals his  dismissive feelings towards tiffany this  results in serious relationship issues  as chucky electrocutes tiffany in her  own bathtub then as a spiteful act he  utilizes the series recurring voodoo  curse to trap tiffany's soul in another  doll the plastic duo then tricks a young  couple jesse and jade into transporting  them to new jersey along the way chucky  and tiffany spill a fair amount of blood  and rekindle their undoubtedly twisted  but endearing romance sadly the  honeymoon doesn't last long and chucky  starts to severely criticize tiffany's  domestic skills  what would martha stewart say martha  stewart  tiffany was so well received by child's  play fans that she was brought back for  three additional sequels  beware the stare of mary shaw she had no  children only dolls and if you see her  in your dreams be sure you never ever  scream whether it's billy from saw or  annabelle from the conjuring director  james wan clearly has a fascination with  dolls and puppets but the precedent for  this recurring trend in his work was set  back in his third theatrical release  dead silence the film follows jamie  ashton who after the death of his wife  returns to his hometown for answers  answers concerning a mysterious  ventriloquist doll and the infamous  local legend about a woman known as mary  shaw she was a renowned ventriloquist  who didn't take kindly to a rude child  interrupting her act and saying that he  could see her lips move  who said  i did i can see it her lips are moving  when the child mysteriously goes missing  the townspeople hunt mary down and kill  her however mary's final wish was  fittingly to be turned into a dummy and  buried with her dolls now in a new  ghostly form complete with soulless eyes  and ventriloquist doll mouth she seeks  vengeance on jaime's bloodline  throughout mary's long reign of terror  she leaves a disgusting trademark on her  victims she rips their tongues out and  gives them horrific puppet-like scars on  their faces  now  who's the dummy  the loved ones is often regarded as an  underrated gem from the past 15 years of  horror cinema the film centers around a  high schooler named brent who ends up in  the crosshairs of his demented classmate  lola after declining her offer to go to  prom brent still coping with his  father's death is kidnapped by her he's  then forced into a disturbing mock prom  by lola and her father while he's  mentally and physically tortured lola  played by robin mclevey completely  steals the show her performance rides  the fine line between disturbing and  campy but never once does mick levy go  too over the top lola at no point in the  film sees anything wrong with what she's  doing to brent she just views the  situation in her demented mind as the  perfect prom night with the cutest guy  in school this delusion is aided by her  equally insane and uncomfortably close  father who helps her with this sickening  act the scale of lola and her father's  crimes only increases throughout the  film which takes several bizarre twists  and turns the true terror of lola is  that throughout the entire movie she  could do anything at any moment she goes  from playfully trying to feed brent in  one scene to threatening to horrifically  mutilate him in the next it's a  performance and film that deserves far  more attention  orphan has received a lot of praise and  criticism since it was first released in  2009. however the one thing all viewers  can agree on is that the character of  esther played by isabelle fuhrman is  completely shocking unique and  unforgettable at the beginning of the  film kate and john coleman hope to heal  their strained marriage by adopting a  third child they're both immediately  drawn to a young russian girl named  esther and decide to adopt her things  almost immediately turn sinister as  esther becomes increasingly manipulative  and injures a school bully as her  transgressions evolve she begins to  reveal her true sadistic nature her evil  goal is to remove her adopted mother  entirely from the picture kate  eventually discovers that esther has no  documented records and a lot of people  in her history have ended up six feet  under all of that information however is  upstaged by the big twist that esther  has a rare hormone condition and is  actually a mentally deranged 33 year old  woman  stop talking to me like i'm a child  after the film's original release furman  received accolades for her disturbing  portrayal of esther her performance was  so haunting that fermen with the help of  some special effects will reprise the  role in an upcoming prequel to the film  jordan peel's us has been hailed as one  of the most thoughtful and original  horror films in recent years it's the  story of the wilson family and a  vacation that goes horribly wrong the  mother adelaide portrayed by lupita  nyong'o is on edge almost immediately  due to a childhood trauma that occurred  in the area when she was walking through  a hall of mirrors at a local carnival  she was attacked by a doppelganger of  herself called a tether many years later  that memory has taken on a dangerous new  reality a group of tethers which seem to  be a version of her entire family start  to wreak havoc at the command of their  mother a woman named red a dangerous  duplicate of adelaide red quickly makes  her intentions clear as she regales the  terrified wilsons with a horrific  monologue whenever on screen red speaks  in a haunting and almost withered voice  which only serves to heighten her menace  add to that her thousand-yard stare  physical prowess and unstoppable drive  and it's impossible to not be frightened  by her it's eventually revealed that  adelaide herself is the actual tether  having snatched and swapped places with  her double during their childhood  encounter nyong'o's double performance  truly is an impressive feat and it's  still disappointing to many fans that  she wasn't nominated for an oscar  one of the best characters in rob  zombie's firefly trilogy is baby played  by sherry moon zombie a member of the  disturbing backwoods serial killer cult  gang known as the fireflies flanked by  the likes of otis and captain spalding  it's quite impressive that baby stands  out as the craziest first introduced in  house of 1000 corpses baby is a  hollywood obsessed and overly bubbly  serial killer carrying out all of her  family's heinous deeds with a sense of  glee and a smile on her face moon zombie  has a clear appreciation and  understanding of the role having played  it three times from 2003 to 2019. over  the course of the following films the  devil's rejects and three from hell  baby's insanity would only increase  despite her bloodthirsty and cruel  nature baby still maintains a strangely  enduring charm a recurring theme in rob  zombie's work this is best illustrated  by a delightful scene where baby and  spalding pester otis into stopping for  ice cream baby despite being a  blood-crazed psychopath does seem to  have a lot of affection and appreciation  for her entire criminally insane family  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  horror films are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

